.TH EMAYL 1 "" "EMAYL" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
emayl \- fast, private email client
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B emayl
.SH DESCRIPTION
EMAYL is a graphical email client for any number of accounts, using IMAP and SMTP.
Start it from the applications menu or by typing its name.
It takes no command-line options.
.PP
Remote content in messages is blocked by default. Passwords are kept in the desktop's
password store (GNOME Keyring or KWallet).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/emayl/
The saved copy of your mail, the outbox and drafts.
.TP
.I ~/.config/emayl/
The list of accounts.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/emayl/problems.log
Notes about errors, written only when something goes wrong.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ICED_BACKEND
Set to
.B tiny-skia
to draw the window with the processor instead of the graphics card.
